WEBVTT

00:30.000 --> 00:33.000
All right, dear, you can stay for the weekend.

00:33.000 --> 00:36.000
Yeah, better come home and get some clothes, huh?

00:36.000 --> 00:37.000
All right, bye.

00:40.000 --> 00:41.000
That was Bab.

00:41.000 --> 00:43.000
She's gonna stay at Franny's for the weekend.

00:43.000 --> 00:44.000
She sent her love to you.

00:44.000 --> 00:45.000
Thanks, Dublin.

00:45.000 --> 00:47.000
Boy, that was delicious grub.

00:47.000 --> 00:48.000
Food.

00:48.000 --> 00:49.000
I stand corrected.

00:49.000 --> 00:52.000
That was delicious food grub.

00:52.000 --> 00:53.000
Excuse me, Mom.

00:53.000 --> 00:54.000
I gotta go over to Joyce.

00:54.000 --> 00:55.000
I left my books over there.

00:55.000 --> 00:57.000
No, well, you come right back.

00:57.000 --> 01:00.000
Okay.

01:00.000 --> 01:01.000
Need any help with the dishes, honey?

01:01.000 --> 01:02.000
No, thanks, dear.

01:02.000 --> 01:03.000
You're sweet, though.

01:03.000 --> 01:04.000
Well, if you do, just holler.

01:04.000 --> 01:06.000
You and you'll be glad to pitch in.

01:06.000 --> 01:07.000
Oh.

01:07.000 --> 01:08.000
Oh.

01:08.000 --> 01:09.000
Oh.

01:09.000 --> 01:10.000
Oh.

01:10.000 --> 01:11.000
Oh.

01:11.000 --> 01:12.000
Oh.

01:12.000 --> 01:13.000
Oh.

01:13.000 --> 01:14.000
Oh.

01:14.000 --> 01:15.000
Oh.

01:15.000 --> 01:16.000
Oh.

01:16.000 --> 01:17.000
Oh.

01:17.000 --> 01:18.000
Oh.

01:18.000 --> 01:19.000
Oh.

01:19.000 --> 01:20.000
Oh.

01:20.000 --> 01:21.000
Oh.

01:21.000 --> 01:22.000
Oh.

01:22.000 --> 01:23.000
Oh.

01:23.000 --> 01:24.000
Oh.

01:24.000 --> 01:25.000
Oh.

01:25.000 --> 01:26.000
Oh.

01:26.000 --> 01:27.000
Oh.

01:27.000 --> 01:28.000
Now, don't you start even a wee bit.

01:28.000 --> 01:29.000
I don't want to disturb you.

01:29.000 --> 01:30.000
Oh, you ain't disturbed me, Waldo.

01:30.000 --> 01:31.000
I was just thinking.

01:31.000 --> 01:32.000
Oh, fine.

01:32.000 --> 01:33.000
Then I take the first time.

01:33.000 --> 01:37.000
This morning, I've bagged off a little poem.

01:37.000 --> 01:38.000
You like poetry, don't you?

01:38.000 --> 01:39.000
Oh, I love poetry.

01:39.000 --> 01:40.000
Heh.

01:40.000 --> 01:43.000
I must know 50 Burma shave signs by heart.

01:43.000 --> 01:44.000
Fine.

01:44.000 --> 01:45.000
This is a different type of poem.

01:45.000 --> 01:50.000
You see, I feel the world today is losing sight of true values.

01:50.000 --> 01:52.000
People are getting cynical and bitter.

01:52.000 --> 01:55.000
We're forgetting the two most precious emotions.

01:55.000 --> 01:56.000
What's that?

01:56.000 --> 01:59.000
Love and friendship.

01:59.000 --> 02:02.000
Love and friendship.

02:02.000 --> 02:04.000
Oh, you're so right.

02:04.000 --> 02:05.000
But not me.

02:05.000 --> 02:06.000
I love friendship.

02:06.000 --> 02:07.000
Oh, fine.

02:07.000 --> 02:13.000
This poem symbolizes the need for people of all beliefs, of all faiths, and of all nations

02:13.000 --> 02:15.000
to live together in peace.

02:15.000 --> 02:17.000
That's a very good poem.

02:17.000 --> 02:18.000
Thank you.

02:18.000 --> 02:21.000
Now, I'll read it for you.

02:21.000 --> 02:22.000
55 pages.

02:22.000 --> 02:24.000
Yes, it's all here.

02:24.000 --> 02:25.000
You ready, Mr. Riley?

02:25.000 --> 02:27.000
Yeah, I'm ready.

02:27.000 --> 02:31.000
There was a wise old owl who had a friend, a mouse.

02:31.000 --> 02:33.000
They lived within a hollow tree.

02:33.000 --> 02:37.000
There was a happy house.

02:37.000 --> 02:38.000
Very good point.

02:38.000 --> 02:40.000
An owl living with a mouse.

02:40.000 --> 02:42.000
Democracy.

02:42.000 --> 02:47.000
Now, the mouse was very small, while the owl was much bigger.

02:47.000 --> 02:48.000
Hiya, fellas.

02:48.000 --> 02:51.000
Oh, Mrs. Riley, can I borrow a couple of eggs?

02:51.000 --> 02:53.000
Just stopped in to borrow a couple of eggs.

02:53.000 --> 02:54.000
Yeah, I see.

02:54.000 --> 02:55.000
Go ahead, Waldo.

02:55.000 --> 02:58.000
Oh, well, I better start at the beginning so you don't lose the thread.

02:58.000 --> 03:01.000
Yeah, pick up the thread.

03:01.000 --> 03:04.000
There was a wise old owl who had a friend, a mouse.

03:04.000 --> 03:06.000
They lived within a hollow tree.

03:06.000 --> 03:08.000
There was a happy house.

03:08.000 --> 03:11.000
Who wants to hear that kind of stuff while living in hollow trees?

03:11.000 --> 03:14.000
Believe me, I suffered enough during the housing shortage.

03:14.000 --> 03:15.000
Quiet, Gillis.

03:15.000 --> 03:16.000
This is a poem.

03:16.000 --> 03:18.000
Go ahead, Waldo.

03:18.000 --> 03:19.000
About love and friendship.

03:19.000 --> 03:21.000
The whole world.

03:21.000 --> 03:22.000
That's what I point out here.

03:22.000 --> 03:23.000
It's a waste of time.

03:23.000 --> 03:26.000
The world can't fall in love with each other just like that.

03:26.000 --> 03:28.000
It's got to start in your own house first.

03:28.000 --> 03:29.000
Like this.

03:29.000 --> 03:30.000
Well?

03:30.000 --> 03:32.000
Well, what?

03:32.000 --> 03:33.000
This tie.

03:33.000 --> 03:35.000
This tie is worth every bit of two bucks.

03:35.000 --> 03:37.000
Ain't you going to ask me where I got it?

03:37.000 --> 03:39.000
Why should I ask you where you got it?

03:39.000 --> 03:42.000
What am I, Department Store Detective?

03:42.000 --> 03:44.000
Ha, ha, ha.

03:44.000 --> 03:46.000
Very humorous.

03:46.000 --> 03:50.000
I'd interest you to know, Riley, that my boy Egbert gave me this tie.

03:50.000 --> 03:52.000
Fine, for your birthday.

03:52.000 --> 03:53.000
It ain't my birthday.

03:53.000 --> 03:55.000
He gave it to me because he loved me.

03:55.000 --> 03:57.000
Because I'm a pal to him, that's why.

03:57.000 --> 04:00.000
My boy ain't going to grow up to be no juvenile delinquent.

04:00.000 --> 04:02.000
Because he and me is buddies.

04:02.000 --> 04:03.000
Coronies.

04:03.000 --> 04:06.000
But you and your poor junior, you're perfectly strangers.

04:06.000 --> 04:09.000
My son and I are very close.

04:09.000 --> 04:10.000
Go ahead, Waldo.

04:10.000 --> 04:13.000
There was a wise old owl who had a friend, a mouse.

04:13.000 --> 04:15.000
Owls living with mice.

04:15.000 --> 04:17.000
Stop that communist propaganda.

04:17.000 --> 04:20.000
All I say is, you got to cultivate your boy in his early years.

04:20.000 --> 04:22.000
My boy likes me fine.

04:22.000 --> 04:23.000
Yeah?

04:23.000 --> 04:26.000
Does he ever give you any little presents like my Egbert gives me?

04:26.000 --> 04:28.000
I mean, unexpected presents.

04:28.000 --> 04:30.000
Well, he does.

04:30.000 --> 04:32.000
See? That proves he don't care about you.

04:32.000 --> 04:35.000
Presents don't mean anything. My son thinks the world of me.

04:35.000 --> 04:37.000
He always speaks very nice to me.

04:37.000 --> 04:39.000
Well, naturally the boy is polite to you.

04:39.000 --> 04:41.000
You're giving him free room and board, ain't you?

04:41.000 --> 04:44.000
He likes me for my own sweet self.

04:44.000 --> 04:46.000
I'm sure of it.

04:46.000 --> 04:49.000
He never said anything about not liking me, did he, Waldo?

04:49.000 --> 04:50.000
Of course not.

04:50.000 --> 04:52.000
All I mean is that love starts in the house.

04:52.000 --> 04:54.000
And a father can't take no chances.

04:54.000 --> 04:57.000
My son and I are very good friends.

04:57.000 --> 04:59.000
The Gillis, here are your eggs.

04:59.000 --> 05:00.000
Oh, thanks. Thanks very much.

05:00.000 --> 05:03.000
So, just remember, be a wise old owl.

05:03.000 --> 05:06.000
Because there's a mouse in the house.

05:07.000 --> 05:09.000
He doesn't remember writing it that way.

05:09.000 --> 05:11.000
What's he talking about?

05:11.000 --> 05:13.000
Oh, nothing, Peg. Something about Junior.

05:13.000 --> 05:15.000
What about Junior?

05:15.000 --> 05:17.000
Nothing.

05:21.000 --> 05:23.000
That Gillis is a mental case.

05:24.000 --> 05:26.000
Junior likes me, don't he, Waldo?

05:26.000 --> 05:27.000
Indubitably.

05:27.000 --> 05:30.000
Now, don't worry. You have a very devoted son.

05:30.000 --> 05:32.000
I'm not worried about anything.

05:32.000 --> 05:34.000
What have I got to be worried about?

05:34.000 --> 05:37.000
There was a wise old owl who had a friendly mouse.

05:37.000 --> 05:40.000
They lived within a hollow tree and there was a...

05:40.000 --> 05:41.000
Junior!

05:41.000 --> 05:42.000
Hi, Pa.

05:42.000 --> 05:44.000
Gee, I'm glad you're home.

05:44.000 --> 05:45.000
What's up?

05:45.000 --> 05:46.000
Nothing, Junior.

05:46.000 --> 05:48.000
Missy Ronnie, I'll see you tomorrow.

05:48.000 --> 05:49.000
Oh, okay, Waldo.

05:49.000 --> 05:51.000
Oh, by the way, that was a very good poem.

05:51.000 --> 05:53.000
Oh, thank you very much. Good night.

05:53.000 --> 05:54.000
Good night.

05:54.000 --> 05:57.000
Oh, wait a minute, Junior. I wanted to talk to you.

05:57.000 --> 05:58.000
Anything wrong, Pa?

05:58.000 --> 06:00.000
Oh, no. No, no.

06:00.000 --> 06:03.000
You know, I was just thinking of some boys I know.

06:03.000 --> 06:05.000
You know, offhand, like.

06:05.000 --> 06:09.000
And I was wondering who's your best friend.

06:09.000 --> 06:11.000
Who's my best friend?

06:11.000 --> 06:12.000
Yeah, you know, like.

06:12.000 --> 06:15.000
Well, if you were in a jam, who would you go to?

06:15.000 --> 06:17.000
Oh, you know the answer to that.

06:17.000 --> 06:19.000
Sure, I know it, but I want to hear you say it.

06:19.000 --> 06:21.000
Well, ma, of course.

06:21.000 --> 06:25.000
Well, your mother ain't anything to knock.

06:25.000 --> 06:28.000
But I mean, well, if you had something to tell somebody,

06:28.000 --> 06:30.000
you know, and you couldn't tell her,

06:30.000 --> 06:32.000
then who would you tell?

06:32.000 --> 06:34.000
Well, then I'd tell Egbert Gillis.

06:34.000 --> 06:39.000
You don't get me, Junior.

06:39.000 --> 06:41.000
Now, suppose you couldn't tell Egbert Gillis,

06:41.000 --> 06:44.000
you couldn't tell your mother, and you couldn't tell your sister.

06:44.000 --> 06:48.000
Now, who else would you tell that you love, that you know loves you?

06:48.000 --> 06:50.000
Oh, I get you now.

06:50.000 --> 06:51.000
Sure you do. Who?

06:51.000 --> 06:54.000
Well, I couldn't say it right to your face, Pa.

06:54.000 --> 06:57.000
Oh, I know it's a little embarrassing.

06:57.000 --> 07:00.000
You don't have to say it to my face. I'll turn my back.

07:00.000 --> 07:01.000
Who?

07:01.000 --> 07:04.000
Well, my girl, Marilyn Morris.

07:04.000 --> 07:06.000
Marilyn Morris?

07:06.000 --> 07:07.000
Yeah, that's right.

07:07.000 --> 07:09.000
Marilyn Morris?

07:09.000 --> 07:11.000
Yeah, that reminds me. I gotta go wash up.

07:11.000 --> 07:15.000
I'm taking her to the movie tonight.

07:15.000 --> 07:18.000
Some boy I got likes girls.

07:18.000 --> 07:19.000
Oh, Pa.

07:19.000 --> 07:21.000
Yes, Junior? Is there something you wanted to tell me,

07:21.000 --> 07:22.000
something you forgot to tell me?

07:22.000 --> 07:24.000
Yeah, there is something I forgot.

07:24.000 --> 07:26.000
I know it, I know it. Tell your old father.

07:26.000 --> 07:34.000
I forgot to ask for my allowance.

07:34.000 --> 07:35.000
There it is.

07:35.000 --> 07:37.000
Gee, an extra quarter.

07:37.000 --> 07:43.000
Gee, thanks, Pa.

07:43.000 --> 07:45.000
I'm late for school. So long, Mom.

07:45.000 --> 07:46.000
Bye, dear.

07:46.000 --> 07:47.000
Come on, Pa.

07:47.000 --> 07:51.000
Wait a minute, Junior. Before you go.

07:51.000 --> 07:53.000
Well, what am I doing?

07:53.000 --> 07:57.000
Oh, well go ahead and whistle if you want to whistle.

07:57.000 --> 07:59.000
I didn't want to whistle, Junior. Go ahead to school.

07:59.000 --> 08:01.000
So long.

08:01.000 --> 08:03.000
Well, Peg, do you see how much Junior loves me?

08:03.000 --> 08:05.000
He's too old for all the boys growing up.

08:05.000 --> 08:06.000
He's too old to kiss you.

08:06.000 --> 08:09.000
He's not too old to kiss that Marilyn, huh?

08:09.000 --> 08:10.000
She's a girl.

08:10.000 --> 08:12.000
You can't treat Junior like a baby.

08:12.000 --> 08:14.000
She'll be fourteen on Sunday.

08:14.000 --> 08:15.000
Peg, is Sunday his birthday?

08:15.000 --> 08:19.000
Oh, Riley, don't tell me you forgot the date.

08:19.000 --> 08:20.000
But it can't be Sunday, Peg.

08:20.000 --> 08:22.000
He was born on a Monday.

08:22.000 --> 08:25.000
I remember, because that day I did the washing and you took it easy.

08:25.000 --> 08:26.000
Riley, he was born on Monday,

08:26.000 --> 08:28.000
but this year his birthday falls on Sunday.

08:28.000 --> 08:30.000
Oh, oh.

08:30.000 --> 08:32.000
Peg, I got a great idea.

08:32.000 --> 08:34.000
I'm going to run a big surprise party for Junior.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.000
Dad will want to change his mind about me.

08:36.000 --> 08:37.000
Junior loves you.

08:37.000 --> 08:39.000
You don't have to go to all this trouble.

08:39.000 --> 08:40.000
Well, it's no trouble at all.

08:40.000 --> 08:42.000
All you do is write out some invitations,

08:42.000 --> 08:43.000
invite everybody,

08:43.000 --> 08:45.000
and then you hang up some nice decorations,

08:45.000 --> 08:47.000
and then you make about five pounds of cookies.

08:47.000 --> 08:48.000
And then the day of the party,

08:48.000 --> 08:51.000
Waldo Binney will come over and move around the furniture,

08:51.000 --> 08:52.000
so we'll have more room.

08:52.000 --> 08:53.000
He doesn't mind the trouble at all.

08:53.000 --> 08:55.000
I can see why.

08:55.000 --> 08:56.000
All right, I'll help with the party,

08:56.000 --> 08:58.000
but you better talk to Junior first.

08:58.000 --> 09:00.000
Oh, no, Peg. This has got to be a surprise.

09:00.000 --> 09:01.000
Oh, but you...

09:01.000 --> 09:03.000
Peg, don't argue. My head's made up.

09:03.000 --> 09:04.000
Now promise me you don't tell Junior.

09:04.000 --> 09:05.000
All right, I promise.

09:05.000 --> 09:06.000
That a girl.

09:06.000 --> 09:08.000
This will really do it.

09:08.000 --> 09:09.000
Yes, sir.

09:09.000 --> 09:11.000
That Junior will know now that I ain't just a man

09:11.000 --> 09:12.000
that married his mother.

09:12.000 --> 09:13.000
I'm his father.

09:13.000 --> 09:14.000
Goodbye, Dumbledore.

09:14.000 --> 09:15.000
Goodbye, dear.

09:15.000 --> 09:16.000
I'll give you lunch.

09:16.000 --> 09:17.000
Oh, thanks, Dumbledore.

09:21.000 --> 09:23.000
Happy birthday, Junior.

09:23.000 --> 09:25.000
Oh, that's so well put.

09:25.000 --> 09:27.000
Hey, you painted it beautiful.

09:27.000 --> 09:28.000
Oh, it's fine, dear.

09:28.000 --> 09:29.000
It's beautiful.

09:29.000 --> 09:30.000
Now, Peg, is everything ready?

09:30.000 --> 09:31.000
We ain't got much time.

09:31.000 --> 09:32.000
Yes, dear. Don't be nervous.

09:32.000 --> 09:34.000
The kids won't be here for two hours yet.

09:34.000 --> 09:35.000
There are 12 of them coming.

09:35.000 --> 09:36.000
Oh, that's great.

09:36.000 --> 09:38.000
Waldo, did you get the ice cream?

09:38.000 --> 09:39.000
Yes, Mr. Riley. Six quarts.

09:39.000 --> 09:40.000
It's in the ice box.

09:40.000 --> 09:42.000
Peg, make all the sandwiches and hide them.

09:42.000 --> 09:44.000
They'll be home from Sunday school any minute now,

09:44.000 --> 09:45.000
and we don't want them to catch on.

09:45.000 --> 09:47.000
Well, you better put this somewhere.

09:47.000 --> 09:48.000
Yeah, that's right.

09:48.000 --> 09:49.000
I'll hide it.

09:49.000 --> 09:50.000
I'll hide it in the coat closet.

09:50.000 --> 09:51.000
Good. Be careful the frosting.

09:51.000 --> 10:13.000
Okay.

10:13.000 --> 10:14.000
Hello, boss.

10:14.000 --> 10:17.000
You don't get a bullet for a minute, do you, Junior?

10:17.000 --> 10:18.000
Huh?

10:18.000 --> 10:20.000
Junior, what are you doing home?

10:20.000 --> 10:22.000
Oh, Sunday school that hour.

10:22.000 --> 10:23.000
What's in the box?

10:23.000 --> 10:24.000
It's nothing. Nothing.

10:24.000 --> 10:25.000
It's just a little cake.

10:25.000 --> 10:26.000
Cake?

10:26.000 --> 10:28.000
Yeah, I was passing a bakery shop,

10:28.000 --> 10:30.000
and I felt the urge for a mouthful of cake.

10:30.000 --> 10:32.000
That cake must be a foot high.

10:32.000 --> 10:34.000
Well, I got a big mouth.

10:34.000 --> 10:35.000
No, Junior.

10:35.000 --> 10:36.000
What's this?

10:36.000 --> 10:39.000
Happy birthday to Junior.

10:39.000 --> 10:41.000
Pop, what's the idea?

10:41.000 --> 10:44.000
Well, I might as well tell you.

10:44.000 --> 10:46.000
Can you keep a secret?

10:46.000 --> 10:48.000
Well, sure.

10:48.000 --> 10:52.000
I'm running you a surprise party this afternoon.

10:52.000 --> 10:53.000
Don't tell a soul.

10:53.000 --> 10:55.000
Surprise party?

10:55.000 --> 10:56.000
For me?

10:56.000 --> 10:57.000
Ain't I wonderful?

10:57.000 --> 11:01.000
Oh, Pop, what'd you have to go and do that for?

11:01.000 --> 11:03.000
Well, Junior, it's your birthday.

11:03.000 --> 11:04.000
How many times are you born?

11:04.000 --> 11:06.000
Oh, well, you should have asked me.

11:06.000 --> 11:08.000
Maybe I got other plans for today.

11:08.000 --> 11:11.000
All right, but you can break them for your father.

11:11.000 --> 11:12.000
Well, no, I can't.

11:12.000 --> 11:15.000
I mean, I could, but...

11:15.000 --> 11:18.000
Well, okay.

11:18.000 --> 11:21.000
Well, okay.

11:21.000 --> 11:22.000
Thanks very much.

11:22.000 --> 11:24.000
Oh, gee, Pop, you don't see...

11:24.000 --> 11:25.000
No, that's okay.

11:25.000 --> 11:26.000
I see.

11:26.000 --> 11:28.000
I see too much.

11:28.000 --> 11:29.000
You don't understand, Pop.

11:29.000 --> 11:30.000
I understand, Junior.

11:30.000 --> 11:32.000
You don't have to apologize.

11:32.000 --> 11:34.000
After all, I...

11:34.000 --> 11:37.000
I can't blame you for feeling like you do about me.

11:37.000 --> 11:39.000
You didn't ask for me to be your father.

11:39.000 --> 11:41.000
It was my own idea.

11:41.000 --> 11:44.000
Maybe that's why you cried so much when you were a baby.

11:44.000 --> 11:47.000
Oh, Pop, don't talk like that.

11:47.000 --> 11:50.000
Listen, Junior, you don't have to feel bad about this.

11:50.000 --> 11:52.000
I don't feel bad.

11:52.000 --> 11:54.000
After all, you should be cheerful.

11:54.000 --> 11:56.000
This is your birthday.

11:56.000 --> 11:58.000
Many happy returns to the day.

11:58.000 --> 12:00.000
Thanks, Pop.

12:00.000 --> 12:03.000
I can't understand why Junior isn't hearing this.

12:06.000 --> 12:07.000
Hello?

12:07.000 --> 12:08.000
Who?

12:08.000 --> 12:11.000
Oh, well, that's too bad.

12:11.000 --> 12:13.000
Yeah, I hope you're better soon.

12:13.000 --> 12:14.000
Bye.

12:14.000 --> 12:15.000
Who's that?

12:15.000 --> 12:16.000
Willie Coogan.

12:16.000 --> 12:17.000
He can't come to the party.

12:17.000 --> 12:18.000
He's in bed with a mean guy.

12:18.000 --> 12:19.000
Oh, I see.

12:19.000 --> 12:20.000
I see.

12:20.000 --> 12:21.000
I see.

